WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.960
Titans' first-season finale came with no shortage
of surprises, with mind-bending plot twists

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.420
and an exciting tease of a post-credits scene.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.160
But the episode's dreamlike quality makes
it easy to wonder what really happened.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.200
Confused by it all?

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:13.820
Don't worry.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.340
Let's break down the climax of Titans season
one.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:22.180
Most of the finale is a hallucination brought
on by Trigon, Rachel's supervillain of a father.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:26.190
In this fake reality, Dick Grayson believes
he's married to Dawn, with the two having

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:28.020
a young son and a baby on the way.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.880
Gar and Raven are off at college.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.240
Life seems to be going great for Dick until
Jason Todd arrives in a wheelchair to warn

00:00:34.249 --> 00:00:38.280
Dick that Batman has finally cracked and is
on the verge of turning from a crime-fighter

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.480
to a vengeful murderer.

00:00:39.829 --> 00:00:43.539
Dick returns to Gotham to see if he can stop
his mentor from killing the Joker, but he

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:44.040
fails.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:48.540
Once Batman starts killing, he can't stop,
and everyone in Arkham is on his hit list.

00:00:48.549 --> 00:00:52.870
Dick gives Batman's secret identity to the
GCPD and helps lead a mission to raid his

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:57.370
home, but Batman is ready for them and kills
almost all of the cops, including Kory, who

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.820
appears in this reality as an FBI agent.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.980
Dick then blows the house up and goes after
Batman himself.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:07.430
When Batman reaches out to his old ward for
help, Dick kills him instead, and that's when

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:09.320
the show returns to the real world.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:13.680
Turns out, nothing in Dick's trip to Gotham
was real except for the emotions he felt and

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:14.840
the choices he made.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:19.540
Trigon himself appears in the vision as a
GCPD detective, but none of the other characters

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:21.780
were actually there, it was all in Dick's
head.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.360
Trigon used the Gotham hallucination to possess
Dick.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:29.510
After Dick kills Batman, the show returns
to the same house where we last saw Trigon,

00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:32.020
Raven, and Angela, Raven's biological mother.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:36.280
Dick's eyes are black and sinister, and to
Raven's horror, he appears to be completely

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:37.660
under Trigon's control.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:41.620
But why did Trigon go through the trouble
of toying with Dick before he took him over?

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:46.070
He wasn't just playing with his food, Trigon
needed the Gotham hallucination for his plan

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:46.560
to work.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:48.500
"I offered your friend a path.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:54.360
It wound down many roads, but ultimately,
he chose his own way."

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:59.560
The season's seventh episode ended with Dick
burning his Robin suit, symbolizing his rejection

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:02.760
of the darker urges he faced going after his
parents' killer.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:07.480
Trigon needed to drag Dick back down to that
dark place, and the Gotham hallucination was

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:08.609
his way of doing it.

00:02:08.609 --> 00:02:12.550
He pushed him to the point of committing one
of the darkest acts he could imagine, killing

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:13.420
his own mentor.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.580
Dick didn't really kill Batman, but it felt
real to him, and that was enough.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:21.000
Once he stepped over that line, he opened
the door for Trigon's influence.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.170
At the end of episode 10, Kory and Donna Troy
both try to follow Dick into the house where

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:29.909
Trigon was summoned, but they're blocked by
an invisible barrier.

00:02:29.909 --> 00:02:31.529
Only Dick is allowed to pass through.

00:02:31.529 --> 00:02:34.380
So why did Trigon want Grayson and none of
the others?

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:36.560
Why possess him rather than kill him?

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:41.540
Titans showrunner Greg Walker told TVLine
that Trigon lets Dick into the house specifically

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:46.000
to turn him to his side, and the reason why,
quote, "has a lot to do with [Trigon's] plan

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:46.560
for Rachel."

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:50.939
It suggests that Trigon needs more from his
daughter than to simply have her bring him

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:51.740
into the world.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:54.660
Whatever his master plan is, this is only
the beginning.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:59.520
In the season's second-to-last episode, we
learn that Angela is just as committed to

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:02.719
bringing Trigon into the world as her former
captors were.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:06.180
She doesn't switch sides, she was working
with Trigon all along.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:07.780
"Who's this?"

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:10.360
"Rachel's mother?"

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:12.680
"They look cozy."

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:17.780
The reveal begs the question of why Angela
was being held in the asylum the Titans freed

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:19.859
her from in the season's 7th episode.

00:03:19.859 --> 00:03:24.109
It could be that making Angela appear to be
a prisoner was all a part of the plan, giving

00:03:24.109 --> 00:03:27.360
the Titans a reason to trust her when it turns
out they really shouldn't.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:32.760
Episode 8 of Titans ends with Rachel restoring
Kori's lost memories, which turns out to be

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:34.940
a bad idea when Kori then attacks her.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:39.180
Kori remembers that she's an alien from the
planet Tamaran, sent to Earth for the express

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:42.480
purpose of killing Rachel in order to stop
her from summoning Trigon.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:47.340
But by season's end, Rachel has successfully
brought Trigon into the world; in a way, the

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:48.120
damage is done.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:51.100
Even if Kori wanted to kill Rachel, what would
be the point?

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:55.540
Maybe now she won't have to and can use her
formidable powers to fight Trigon instead.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:04:00.400
For the most part, the real Beast Boy appears
to be absent from the finale, but his presence

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.440
can still be felt in Dick's hallucination.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:06.700
Shortly before Dick leaves for Gotham in his
vision, his son gives him his favorite toy,

00:04:06.709 --> 00:04:09.090
a stuffed tiger, to protect him on his journey.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:13.010
The tiger was a gift from Gar, which is more
than just on brand for the Beast Boy, it could

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:14.510
also have a deeper meaning.

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:18.630
It could be that Gar now has some kind of
psychic connection with Dick, acting as an

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:20.820
antidote of sorts to Trigon's influence.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:25.200
It might be just the sign Dick needs to snap
back to reality in season 2.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:31.100
Episode 9 focuses on Hank and Dawn, aka Hawk
and Dove, showing us their origin story as

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:33.980
Dawn recovers from her fight with the Nuclear
Family.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:38.130
But their flashbacks are curiously interrupted
by calls for help from Rachel, which seem

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.920
to be intruding before they ever met her in
real life.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:41.800
What's going on?

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:45.700
Why did Rachel send her messages into the
past, and how did she do it?

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:49.570
In the comics it was shown as early as her
first appearance that Rachel's psychic powers

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:50.920
could play havoc with time.

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:55.320
It seems likely that the same thing is happening
in Titans, and she might not even know she's

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:55.820
doing it.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:59.000
Either way, the heroes seem to take notice
of her cries for help.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:02.850
When Dawn wakes up in the hospital, she tells
Hank they need to go find Jason Todd.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:06.830
With one Robin under Trigon's control, maybe
teaming up with the second one can help turn

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:07.560
things around.

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:12.320
The last moments of the season finale feature
the potential introduction of two more DC

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:15.140
heroes, and they might just change the show's
whole dynamic.

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:19.630
The scene features a naked figure, hidden
in shadows, raging through Cadmus Laboratories

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:23.620
in Metropolis, with dead or dying scientists
sprawled out across the floor.

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:27.940
As the man opens up a cage to free a dog,
he shows a telltale "S" symbol.

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:31.360
Just before the screen goes black, the dog's
eyes glow bright red.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:35.940
It's all but certain that the naked man and
his dog are none other than Superboy and Krypto.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:39.940
While DC Comics have had multiple characters
with the name of Superboy, one of them was

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:43.080
Kon-El, a clone of Superman developed by Cadmus
Labs.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:45.710
How would he and Krypto play into season 2?

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:49.680
That's still a mystery, one that will probably
have to wait until Dick is back on the side

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:50.320
of 
the light.

